note mutant: gate.om with exactly one line replaced, compiled to ST/nm; true when built
fn mutant nm view uchar * a view uchar * b view uchar * to bool
sset SP tgateom
ok = fload SP
sset SA a
sset SB b
sclr SBLK
c = xf 0 SA SB SBLK
if ne c 1
sset SM tcfail
sx SM nm
sx SM tcl1
sx SM a
sx SM tcnu
say 1 SM
cbad
ret false
end
ctmp SD nm
sx SD tdotom
ok = fsavc SD
ctmp SH2 nm
sx SH2 tsrcom
rc = gcomp SOMG SD SH2
if ne rc 0
sset SM tcfail
sx SM nm
sx SM tcmdb
say 1 SM
cbad
ret false
end
scp SLST SH2
ret true
end

note a kill is the mutant's own verdict code want; any other exit (spawn failure 1000, signal
note 256+n, exec failure 127, an unrelated refusal) is an infrastructure failure, never a kill
fn mres nm view uchar * survived bool rc ulong want ulong to void
if survived
sset SM tcfail
sx SM nm
sx SM tcsurv
say 1 SM
cbad
ret
end
if ne rc want
sset SM tcfail
sx SM nm
sx SM tcinfra
sn SM rc
sx SM tcwant
sn SM want
sx SM tcend
say 1 SM
cbad
ret
end
sset SM tcpass
sx SM nm
sx SM tckill
sx SM tcexit
sn SM rc
sx SM tcend
say 1 SM
end

